(1.1 Linear Equations) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 664 Tm
(A linear equation in n variables has the form:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 648 Tm
(  a1*x1 + a2*x2 + ... + an*xn = b) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 632 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 616 Tm
(A system of linear equations is a collection of one or more) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 600 Tm
(linear equations involving the same variables.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 584 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 568 Tm
(Example system \(2 equations, 2 unknowns\):) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 552 Tm
(  2x + 3y = 8) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 536 Tm
(  x - y = 1) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 520 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 504 Tm
(Solution Methods:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 488 Tm
(  - Substitution: solve one equation, substitute into other) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 472 Tm
(  - Elimination: add/subtract equations to eliminate variables) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 456 Tm
(  - Matrix methods: Gaussian elimination, Cramer's rule) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 440 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 424 Tm
(1.2 Gaussian Elimination) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 408 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 392 Tm
(Steps:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 376 Tm
(  1. Write augmented matrix [A|b]) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 360 Tm
(  2. Use row operations to reach row echelon form:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 344 Tm
(     - Swap two rows) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 328 Tm
(     - Multiply a row by a nonzero scalar) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 312 Tm
(     - Add a multiple of one row to another) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 296 Tm
(  3. Back-substitute to find the solution) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 280 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 264 Tm
(Row Echelon Form:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 248 Tm
(  - All zero rows at the bottom) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 232 Tm
(  - Leading entry \(pivot\) of each row is to the right) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 216 Tm
(    of the pivot in the row above) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 200 Tm
(  - All entries below pivots are zero) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 184 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 168 Tm
(Solution Types:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 152 Tm
(  - Unique solution: one solution exists) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 136 Tm
(  - Infinitely many: free variables exist) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 120 Tm
(  - No solution: inconsistent system \(0 = nonzero\)) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 104 Tm
() Tj
